# Subscriptions

Package tiers are the hard upper bound on access. See `permissions.mdc` for the effective-access formula.

## Tiers

- `Free`: `app_shell`, `auth_session`, `general_settings`, `patient_registry`, `reports_audit`.
- `Basic`: Free plus tenant, facility, access admin, rooms/beds, OPD, triage, clinical, limited IPD, pharmacy dispense, billing, communications.
- `Advanced`: Basic plus full IPD, nursing, discharge, emergency, lab, radiology, physiotherapy, pharmacy clinical, claims, and reports.
- `Pro`: Advanced plus ICU, theater, HR, biomedical, operations, housekeeping, mortuary, integrations, and dental when enabled.
- `Custom`: Tenant-specific subset or extension of Pro; every entitlement must be explicit.
- `Developer`: Non-production only; may include `demo_seed` manage.

## Enforcement

- Package checks must run in UI and API paths.
- Grants must never exceed the active package.
- Package changes, resets, upgrades, and downgrades must be atomic and auditable.
- Failed changes must roll back completely.

